			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1608832">
									

<p>Well, from what I understand, the price is something happening to you that causes you as much pain as you were receiving benefit. So, longer life would have to be balanced by something pretty bad happening to you. It's not so much how bad 738 getting loose as it is how bad Michaelson losing his body is.</p>
<p>I thought of it this way:</p>
<p>Healed = +1<br />
Longer life = +Eleventy billion</p>
<p>Healed + Longer life = -Eleventy billion - 1</p>
<p>And the only thing that could really offset that is a PROFOUND loss.</p>
<p>EDIT: In case I wasn't being clear, I consider having your lifespan increased to be the ultimate good thing.</p>

